# Shell scripts keep LF line endings even on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true),
# otherwise bash fails on the carriage returns.
*.sh text eol=lf

# From Claude Code Game Studios' own .gitattributes (adopted 2026-10-26), same reasons:
# awk programs read with `awk -f` (mawk/BWK awk may misread CRLF):
*.awk text eol=lf
# a pattern list Claude Code reads when it makes a worktree (CRLF would end every pattern in \r):
.worktreeinclude text eol=lf
# tabular data compared byte-for-byte with generated (LF) output:
*.tsv text eol=lf
# Markdown under .claude/ is authored LF (tooling substring-matches sentences across lines):
.claude/**/*.md text eol=lf
